Build=0.31.0.0; CLR=2.0.50727.8806; OS=Microsoft Windows NT 6.1.7601 Service Pack 1
Manual boxes (color reference coordinates): M2=default; M1=default; Search=automatic; Measure=automatic
Export/startup UTC=2026-10-27T02:36:59.2343780Z
Source update interval approximately 60 seconds; polls and fresh-image confirmation use newly downloaded source bytes.
Poll=60s; stale=240s; CHECK IMAGE=4 fresh consecutive frames; scene_min=0.6800; day_sky_max=35.00; on_fraction=0.003000; off_fraction=0.001000; red_min=30
Base region=x=0.58500, y=0.19000, w=0.18000, h=0.10000
Sound=True; Toast=True

Active reference index 0=supplied-off.png; index 1=curve-view.jpg
decisions/: UTC decision records, measurements, gates, confirmation counts, and alert/toast reasons. Sessions have unique IDs.
frames/: exact downloaded source bytes, linked by source_frame and SHA256 in decisions. Duplicates reuse a frame. TEST mode is marked.
references/: supplied scene references and any saved OFF reference. Reference index 0 is the active OFF reference; index 1 is the supplied curve scene when loaded.
Retention: latest 60 unique snapshots, capped at 20 MiB; latest 6 decision logs rotating near 4 MiB each. Older records may reference frames already expired.
Every confirmed status transition can toast. Initial baseline and unchanged status do not toast. Pending CHECK IMAGE does not toast; 4 fresh consecutive uncertain images confirm it.
WEST CURVE TRAIN, M2 TRAIN and M1 TRAIN are dashboard-only labels. WEST CURVE TRAIN requires a located bright-obstruction gate and new narrow or sparse branched white light intersecting the registered curve signal area. Faint/different color alone cannot produce it. White-shape acceptance/rejection is logged. It does not infer travel direction from a still image. M1 and M2 use the same wider-picture foreground comparison against labeled examples, aligned using separate static background landmarks. Train appearance never depends on the signal ROI, signal lock, or a red signal reflection. Strong matches require similarity >=0.78 and M1/M2 separation >=0.06. A second path permits similarity >=0.70 only with separation >=0.20, winning background score >=0.90 and >=300 foreground pixels. Both paths retain scene and foreground-extent checks. These are similarity thresholds, not recognition probabilities. Signal state, confirmation count and toast text are unchanged.
Daylight requires a confirmed scene, a bright registered sky patch, and a solar-clock elevation of at least -3 degrees at La Plata using PC UTC time. Unconfirmed camera views display PTZ OUT OF RANGE and retain CHECK IMAGE confirmation semantics. The printed timestamp is never read.
Sound requests cannot prove audible playback. Daylight is silent. No OCR or camera timestamp recognition. Age uses HTTP Last-Modified and duplicate bytes.
Background scene matching relocates the search after pan/zoom using at least two matching landmark patches. Show boxes / Hide boxes toggles all debugging outlines and M1/M2 sample labels, including the adjacent actual color samples and search/measurement outlines. Hidden by default; preference is saved. Recognition continues while hidden. Yellow watch box includes nearby upper/lower groups; inner analysis area retains established glare/change gates. Color quadrant counts do not identify aspects, heads, or M1/M2. The separate experimental color bar uses user-labeled M2-left/M1-right zones with independent scene registration. Colors are reflected-color estimates; upper/lower head order is intentionally not inferred. Color readings do not change alert state, confirmation, sound, blink or toast. Polling is fixed at 60 seconds.
This ZIP contains camera images and diagnostic details. Review it before sharing. Export stays on your computer.
Startup note: 

